# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.spyderproject
.ropeproject

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `mkdocs build` output. The docs themselves are plain Markdown under docs/ and
# are the source of truth; the site is a convenience.
site/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Several conventional Python and data-science .gitignore templates would break
# this repo. If you paste one in, keep these tracked:
#
#   data/telco_churn.csv    the real-data cross-check in 01. Templates that
#                           ignore data/ or *.csv silently disable section 7.
#   docs/images/*.png       the figures the README embeds. outputs/ is ignored,
#                           so without these the README is a page of broken
#                           images on GitHub.
#   docs/sample_run.txt     the committed console transcript.
#   part_a_metrics.ipynb    committed with outputs; see the Jupyter note above.
#   policies/*.yaml         the decision layer. It is configuration, but it is
#                           source, and its versions appear in the audit trail.
#   docs/images/*.svg       hand-authored diagrams. They are text, and they are
#                           meant to be diffed and reviewed like code.
#   docs/claims.md          generated, but committed: CI diffs it to catch a
#                           ledger that was edited without being re-rendered.
